        "claim": "Entropy weights put light intensity first at 18.99 percent; the four region types then score 0.0535, 0.1747, 0.3596, and 0.8730, and of the three graded strategies the energy plan cuts Tosca by 4.80 to 11.65 percent while urban planning cuts Latsia by 3.26 to 7.51 percent.",
        "support_steps": [
          "Build the score from four pillars and nine sub-indicators",
          "Let the entropy of the data set the weights",
          "Represent each region type by its cluster center",
          "Grade each strategy by the share of the gap it closes",
          "Keep the strategy with the widest reduction"
        ],
        "decision_consequence": "Audit and dim Tosca's lighting, and replan Latsia's roads and buildings.",
        "source_pages": [
          9,
          12,
          20,
          21
        ]
      }
    ],
